  "ALL_TEXT": "114 INT. POLICE STATION - DAY \nThe sparsely filled stationed is manned by VEERAYYA, who is \non the phone, and a couple of constables. VEDA, GOVARDHAN and \nSULOCHANA are stuck in the cell, desperate and helpless. \nVEERAYYA \nMari station lo unna aa pillalu? \nSUBBA RAJU (O.S.) \nChuddam...Aedokati cheddam... \nVEDA is holding on to the bars of the cell, screaming. \nGOVARDHAN stands next to him. SULOCHANA sits in the corner of \nthe cell. \nGOVARDHAN \nVaddhu! Champoddhu!... Meme \nchampamaamu ani cheppamante \nchepthaamu...Jailo anna \nbrathikundocchu... \nVEDA \nMaakem theleedu... mammalni \nencounter cheyyoddu... \nSULOCHANA starts sobbing. VEERAYYA stands next to the cell \nbars, points his phone to the cell, and talks to the trio. \nVEERAYYA \nEncounter chesthaam ani \nevarannaarayya? \nVEERAYYA \nMeeremanna naxalites aa \ncheyataaniki...ikkada meeru undatam \nsafe kadaani jail maarusthunnam... \nVEDA \nLedu!...Mammalni vadilinatte vadili \nvenakanundi shoot chesthaaru... \nNaaku thelusu... \nVEERAYYA \nIdigo naaku mimmalni bathilaade \ntime ledu... vasthaara naalugu \npeeki theesukellamantaara? \nGOVARDHAN \nVEDA aayana maata vinaku... \nbayapadaku...dhebbalu padthe \npaddai, nuvvu maatram aa rodlu \nodhalaku. \nSUBBA RAJU is listening to it from the phone. VEERAYYA puts \nthe phone back in his ear. \nVEERAYYA \nAppatinundi idhe gola saar... \nSUBBA RAJU (O.S.) \n(sighs) \nSarle...poddhunnundi bhayam tho \nchasthunnattunaaru... nenu vachi \nmaatlaadutha... cell lo unna \nmigitha iddarini vadileyyi. \nHe hangs up the call. VEDA and GOVARDHAN are still clinging \nand staring in horror as VEERAYYA opens the cell. He asks the \nother two inmates, one of whom is the BUM, to get up and \nleave. Seeing this, VEDA and GOVARDHAN start wailing even \nharder. A constable, the only other person in the station, is \nat the entrance, not bothered about what happens inside. The \nBUM picks up the briefcase and leaves. \nGOVARDHAN \nVaallanenduku pampichesaaru??? \nSaakshaalavvuthaarana... Lockup lo \nne champesetattunnaaru! \nVEDA \nSir... champoddu sir... memu \npaaripomu sir... maakem theleedu \nsir... kaavaalante anni oppesukuni \nedella siksha veyandi saar... \nchampoddu sir. \nSULOCHANA starts weeping. \nVEERAYYA \n(Walks away) \nBha! Chepthe vine paristhithi lo \nleru... yedavani koncham sepu. \nHe calls the constable from outside and gives him some money \nVEERAYYA \nBiryani theesukura...nuvvu thinesi \nmaaku theesukura... late aina \nparvaledu. \nGOVARDHAN \n118. \nAyyooo!! Constable ni kuda \npampichesaadu... Ayyo! \nVEDA \nSaaaar!.. Pleaase saar!.. Please \nsaar!! \n(Pointing at SULOCHANA) \nPaapam ammayi saar... please saar. \nVEERAYYA has had enough by now. \nVEERAYYA \nNoru musukuntaara koncham sepu!.. \nYem cheyyananni chepthunnaanu ga! \nNannu chusthe encounter chestha \nanipisthunada?? \nVEDA \nMimmalni chusthe anipiyyatledu \nsaar... Saar ni chusthe \nanipisthundi saar... Please saar... \nmammalnodileyandi saar... Champoddu \nsaar. \nVEERAYYA \nBha! Cheppina ardham kaadayya \nmeeku... yedupugottu yedavalu. \nGOVARDHAN \nPoni kaneesam noppi lekunda anna \nchampandi saar... \nVEDA \nBudhunda? Champoddhani nenu \nbathilaaduthunte noppi lekunda \nchampamantaav... adi tharavaatha \naadaalsina beram, ippude \nmodalupettaku nuvvu. \nVEDA turns towards VEERAYYA. \nVEDA \nSaar!...aayana maatalu vinakandi \nsaar!!! Champoddu saar. \nSUBBA RAJU walks in to the station, slightly amused. \nSUBBA RAJU \nMeeru vellochu... \nVEERAYYA has a faint smile on his face. The three walk out \nwith trepidation. They turn back and see SUBBA RAJU, still in \nshock. SUBBA RAJU turns and talks towards VEERAYYA. \nSUBBA RAJU \n\\Case close cheyyali... paper work \nchaala untadi... Thellarangaane \nPrasad ni pilipinchi paperwork \nfinish cheyinchandi. \nVEERAYYA \nAlaage andi. \nSUBBA RAJU \nSHAM GOPAL VERMA garu ramanaru. \nNenu bayaluderutha. \nSUBBA RAJU leaves. The trio stand in the middle of the \nstation, too afraid to move. VEERAYYA picks up some papers \nand files from SUBBA RAJU's table and puts them in a shelf. \nThe three feel a little weird at how very little attention is \nnow being paid to them. VEDA slowly turns his foot towards \nthe door and tries to put one step forward. He looks at \nVEERAYYA to see if he would notice. VEERAYYA is not bothered, \nbusy with his work. Slowly, VEDA takes another step forward. \nSULOCHANA and GOVARDHAN follow him cautiously. GOVARDHAN then \nstarts to go back, towards his tiffin box and water flask. \nVEDA is peeved at him. \nVEDA \n(Harsh Whisper) \nAtetu!!? Itra!!.. \nGOVARDHAN \n(Whisper) \nNaa tiffin box! \nVEDA bites his teeth to control his anger. SULOCHANA puts her \nhand on his shoulder and calms him down. GOVARDHAN tip-toes \nto his stuff and picks them up. Just as he turns back, \nVEERAYYA turns to look at them... The three freeze in their \ntracks. VEERAYYA is just staring at them. \nVEERAYYA \n(Confused) \n...Enti? \nThe three don't say anything. VEERAYYA turns away, muttering \nto himself. The three walk to the exit, very, very, very \nslowly constantly looking over their back. They almost exit, \nwhen VEERAYYA comes and aims a gun at them. The three freeze \nin their tracks, choked with fear and huddled close to each \nother with tightly shut eyes. VEERAYYA's looks serious... A \ntense three seconds pass... then VEERAYYA chuckles and gets \nback to his paperwork. \nCUT TO:",
